<InfoPage
  title="Privacy"
  eyebrow="Effective August 2, 2026"
  lede="Agewell Brief collects only the information needed to operate the publication, understand basic site performance, and deliver services a reader requests."
>
  <h2>Information readers provide</h2>
  <p>When newsletter enrollment is enabled, we collect the email address submitted by the reader and the consent record associated with that subscription. Messages sent to us contain the address and information the sender chooses to provide.</p>

  <h2>Technical information</h2>
  <p>Our hosting and security providers may process ordinary request information such as IP address, browser type, requested page, timestamp, and security signals. This information supports delivery, abuse prevention, reliability, and aggregate performance measurement.</p>

  <h2>How information is used</h2>
  <p>We use information to deliver requested emails, operate and secure the site, respond to correspondence, understand publication performance, and meet legal obligations. We do not sell reader contact information.</p>

  <h2>Service providers and external links</h2>
  <p>Cloudflare provides site hosting, delivery, and security. Newsletter and analytics providers will be named here when those services are activated. Links to source publishers, advertisers, and affiliate destinations lead to sites with their own privacy practices.</p>

  <h2>Reader choices</h2>
  <p>Every marketing email will include an unsubscribe path. Readers may ask about, correct, or request deletion of information associated with them through our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>

  <h2>Updates</h2>
  <p>We will update this notice when our data practices or service providers change and revise the effective date above.</p>
</InfoPage>
